    </div><div class="disclaimer-strip">This website presents selected supplier opportunities from Primorsky Krai and the Russian Far East. Product availability, import eligibility, documentation, pricing and delivery terms are confirmed separately for each inquiry.</div></section>

    <section class="due-diligence-section" id="due-diligence"><div class="due-diligence-inner"><div class="due-diligence-copy"><p class="eyebrow">FOR PHILIPPINE IMPORTERS &amp; BUSINESS PARTNERS</p><h2>Planning to sign a contract with a Russian supplier?</h2><p class="due-lead">Before starting cooperation, Philippine companies can request an independent background review of a Russian supplier or business partner.</p><p class="due-lead">We help collect and analyse publicly available information about the company, including its registration status, business history, legal disputes, bankruptcy indicators, enforcement proceedings and other available signs of counterparty reliability.</p><div class="due-accent">The review can be requested not only for suppliers presented through Russia–Philippines Trade Link, but also for a Russian company independently selected by the Philippine buyer.</div><h3>What the review may cover</h3><ul class="due-list"><li><svg class="icon"><use href="#check"></use></svg><span>Company registration and current legal status</span></li><li><svg class="icon"><use href="#check"></use></svg><span>Founders, directors and ownership information where publicly available</span></li><li><svg class="icon"><use href="#check"></use></svg><span>Company operating history and basic business profile</span></li><li><svg class="icon"><use href="#check"></use></svg><span>Arbitration and court cases</span></li><li><svg class="icon"><use href="#check"></use></svg><span>Bankruptcy and enforcement information</span></li><li><svg class="icon"><use href="#check"></use></svg><span>Signs of liquidation, reorganisation or suspended activity</span></li><li><svg class="icon"><use href="#check"></use></svg><span>Public financial and business-risk indicators</span></li><li><svg class="icon"><use href="#check"></use></svg><span>Available export experience and product information</span></li><li><svg class="icon"><use href="#check"></use></svg><span>Comparison of the supplier’s declared information with available public records</span></li></ul><div class="due-result"><strong>What you receive</strong>The client receives a structured background summary with identified risk factors, open questions and practical points to clarify before signing a contract or making an advance payment.</div><p class="due-note">This is an independent information review based on available public and legally accessible sources. It is not a government certificate, legal opinion, audit or guarantee of future performance. Findings are framed as risk indicators, information gaps and points requiring additional verification.</p></div><div class="due-diligence-panel"><form id="due-diligence-form" class="due-form" action="mailto:rus.import.ph@gmail.com" method="get"><h3>Request a Counterparty Check</h3><p class="due-form-intro">Send your company name, contact person and preferred way to reach you. We will clarify the remaining details in a follow-up.</p><label for="due-company">Philippine company name<input id="due-company" name="Philippine company name" autocomplete="organization" placeholder="Your company" required></label><label for="due-contact">Contact person<input id="due-contact" name="Contact person" autocomplete="name" placeholder="Your name" required></label><label for="due-contact-details">Phone or email<input id="due-contact-details" name="Phone or email" autocomplete="email" placeholder="Phone number or email address" required></label><button class="button button-primary" type="submit">Request a Counterparty Check <svg class="icon"><use href="#arrow"></use></svg></button><small>We review publicly available and legally accessible information only. We do not promise access to closed databases, bank information or confidential law-enforcement data.</small></form><div class="due-sources"><strong>Possible public sources may include</strong><ul><li>Russian state registration and tax records</li><li>Public court and arbitration records</li><li>Bankruptcy and enforcement databases</li><li>Public corporate and business databases, including SPARK or SBIS where access is available</li><li>Company websites, official documents and open business information</li><li>Other legally accessible public sources</li></ul><p>Reports avoid categorical conclusions such as “fraudulent company”. They identify available signals, open questions and matters that may require enhanced due diligence or independent legal and financial verification.</p></div></div></div></section>

    <section class="dark-section" id="how-it-works"><div class="dark-intro"><p class="eyebrow eyebrow-light">A PRACTICAL START</p><h2>From a product request<br>to a serious conversation.</h2><p>The first goal is not to promise a deal. It is to find out whether the product, documentation, price and market fit make a deal worth discussing.</p></div><div class="steps-grid">
      <div class="step"><span class="step-number">01</span><h3>Send an inquiry</h3><p>Tell us what product, volume and supply format you are looking for.</p></div><div class="step"><span class="step-number">02</span><h3>Supplier matching</h3><p>We identify a suitable manufacturer from Primorsky Krai and request current information.</p></div><div class="step"><span class="step-number">03</span><h3>Document check</h3><p>We clarify specifications, export documents, packaging, pricing basis and market requirements.</p></div><div class="step"><span class="step-number">04</span><h3>Direct negotiation</h3><p>The buyer and supplier discuss commercial terms, samples, logistics and a possible trial shipment.</p></div>
    </div></section>

    <section class="contact-section" id="contact"><div class="contact-copy"><p class="eyebrow">START A CONVERSATION</p><h2>Have a product<br><em>in mind?</em></h2><p>Send the basic details. We will assess what information is needed and whether a suitable supplier can be identified.</p><div class="contact-details"><a href="mailto:rus.import.ph@gmail.com"><svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#mail"></use></svg> rus.import.ph@gmail.com</a><a href="https://wa.me/639215884430"><svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#message"></use></svg> WhatsApp business inquiries</a><a href="viber://chat?number=%2B639215884430"><svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#message"></use></svg> Viber business inquiries</a><span><svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#pin"></use></svg> Republic of the Philippines</span></div></div><form id="inquiry-form" class="inquiry-form" action="mailto:rus.import.ph@gmail.com" method="get" aria-describedby="inquiry-consent"><label for="inquiry-type">Inquiry type<select id="inquiry-type" name="Inquiry type" required><option value="">Select an inquiry type</option><option>Product sourcing</option><option>Supplier introduction</option><option>Russian counterparty check</option><option>Other business inquiry</option></select></label><label for="company">Company name<input id="company" name="Company" autocomplete="organization" placeholder="Your company" required></label><label for="contact">Contact person<input id="contact" name="Contact" autocomplete="name" placeholder="Your name" required></label><label for="product">Product or category<input id="product" name="Product" autocomplete="off" placeholder="What are you looking for?" required></label><label for="volume">Required volume<input id="volume" name="Volume" autocomplete="off" placeholder="Estimated volume or frequency"></label><label for="message">Message<textarea id="message" name="Message" rows="4" placeholder="Packaging, delivery point or any other details"></textarea></label><button class="button button-primary" type="submit">Send inquiry <svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#arrow"></use></svg></button><small id="inquiry-consent">By sending an inquiry, you agree that we may use the information to respond to your business request.</small></form></section>
